WEBVTT

00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:07,140
Hello, everybody. This is Dr. Kevin Cutters and in this video in this section of our website, we're going to talk about

00:00:07,540 --> 00:00:09,540
gastrointestinal cancers.

00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:15,860
Now your GI system really starts in the mouth and ends where you deposit

00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:22,420
feces in the toilet, but in this section, we're really going to talk about the cancers from your stomach

00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:30,340
down. Now your GI cancers are named after the area that the cancer has found

00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:36,100
and the cell type that the cancer has found. It's important to understand when we're talking about

00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:42,740
any cancer. If I have rectal cancer and it metastasizes to my liver, it's not liver cancer. Now it's

00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:49,540
still rectal cancer that's metastasized to my liver, so it's still those cells that cell type

00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:57,380
of the original spot, that origin of the cancer that is metastasized. So liver cancer is cancer of

00:00:57,380 --> 00:01:04,180
the liver cells, rectal cancer or another cancer is cancer of those other cells that may

00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:10,660
metastasize to a different area. So we can have metastasized cancer to the GI tract. Then it's not

00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:16,820
primary. It's secondary. It's metastasized cancer. So in this section we're talking about primary

00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:26,100
GI cancers of the stomach on down. So those are named after the cell type that is found in the biopsy

00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:33,540
and named after the area of where the primary cancer was found, whether it's small intestine,

00:01:33,540 --> 00:01:40,900
gastric cancer, anal cancer, appendiceal cancer and so on. Now it can be very difficult when you get

00:01:40,900 --> 00:01:47,940
a diagnosis of any type of cancer on deciding what to do. Many people are hurting down a pathway that

00:01:48,740 --> 00:01:57,780
quite frankly they may regret dial the road. My recommendation for everybody, when you

00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:03,460
get a diagnosis of cancer, it's very scary. I know I've been there, but when you get a diagnosis of

00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:13,380
cancer, the best thing to do is to slow down. Don't make any rash judgments and grave decisions that

00:02:13,380 --> 00:02:20,100
you may want to. There's nothing you can do to change if you go into surgery. It's done. You can't

00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:26,580
undo that. So you can always do surgery. You can always do chemo. You can always do radiation,

00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:31,940
but you always have more time than usually than what you're told. Not that you're supposed to stick

00:02:31,940 --> 00:02:37,860
your head on the sand and pretend it's not there, but slow down. Take a little time do some research.

00:02:38,500 --> 00:02:46,100
It's also important to understand that when you're considering chemo, radiation, surgery or whatever

00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:52,980
else that you can also do alternative care at the same time. And quite frankly that's probably

00:02:52,980 --> 00:02:59,620
going to be your best bet to help improve the outcome. I'm not against doing chemo, radiation,

00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:06,180
surgery or immunotherapy or something combination thereof. If it's the right thing for you,

00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:12,900
but I think it's probably kind of silly not to make some dietary changes and look at nutrition

00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:21,620
and look at other therapeutic interventions, aka alternative care, that would be wise to help you,

00:03:21,620 --> 00:03:27,220
even if you do choose to do chemo or radiation or something, it'll help you get through that much

00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:32,740
better. So that's all I'm asking you to do. And really that's what our whole website is all about.

00:03:32,740 --> 00:03:39,300
And that's why we give away my books on this site too. So navigate to the free books, download them,

00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:45,300
they're free. Not everybody's ever going to be able to come to us, but we feel like we want this

00:03:45,940 --> 00:03:52,580
clinic to be as much of a ministry as possible so that you can gain knowledge. We are called by God

00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:59,700
to not be foolish and not be ignorant. And of course that's talking about scriptural things,

00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:06,020
but it's also talking about how we live our lives or the decisions that we're making that change

00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:14,340
it all through our life. So adding alternative care to standards of care or doing alternative care

00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:19,780
prior to doing standards of care so maybe that you won't need to do that standard of care that

00:04:19,780 --> 00:04:25,540
they're recommending, at least look into it. That's what this is all about. And when you do look into it,

00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:32,020
I know it is confusing. Should I take, you know, this supplement or that supplement or eat this food

00:04:32,020 --> 00:04:38,500
or use this type of therapy? Well, please use this in this website as best you can to gain as much

00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:45,140
knowledge as you can. And if you do feel led to schedule a case review with me so that we can talk about

00:04:45,140 --> 00:04:53,460
it. Ultimately, we want you to have the best results possible, the best outcome possible from this

00:04:53,460 --> 00:05:03,060
diagnosis. And that's really what our goal is for you. So utilize this site, utilize our free

00:05:03,060 --> 00:05:07,060
material and please be blessed by it. We're always here for you.

